{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-120",
  "title": "Initial Concepts",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Initial Concepts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**1. the guide** *(clear, direct, trustworthy)*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "focus: making it easy for someone to get the help they need. no fluff, no distractions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "visual approach: clean, bold typography, high contrast but not aggressive, maybe a strong directional element (arrows, paths, wayfinding cues)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "who it speaks to: people in crisis who need a lifeline, and staff who need a workspace that doesn’t drain them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**2. the amplifier** *(empowering, energetic, bold)*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "focus: giving foster youth a *voice*, making them feel heard and seen, and showing that this office isn’t passive—it *fights* for them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "visual approach: dynamic shapes, overlapping layers (symbolizing different voices coming together), high-impact colors (maybe jewel tones for richness, not just primary colors)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "who it speaks to: youth who want to feel like they have some power in this system, and staff who want to feel like what they do actually matters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**3. the bridge** *(warm, welcoming, personal)*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "focus: making the office feel human, like a safe place where people aren’t just a case number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "visual approach: friendly type, softer edges (maybe rounded sans-serifs), hand-drawn or organic elements, warm colors that suggest care rather than bureaucracy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "who it speaks to: youth who are nervous to reach out and need reassurance, and staff who want to feel like they’re part of something supportive, not just another cog in the machine."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "each of these directions has a different emotional pull, but all of them work for an office like this. depends on whether they want to lean into clarity, empowerment, or warmth."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}